#   (default) outbound: the source of the rule is in zone Host, and a rule of Network Firewall names no zone: give the networks behind Host with --zone-network; the destination of the rule is in zone Domain, Public, and a rule of Network Firewall names no zone: give the networks behind Domain, Public with --zone-network

echo 'Done. Associate the policy with a firewall when you are ready; until then nothing changes.' >&2
